---
name: view-card-shape
description: |-
  Update box-local custom views (views/*.tsx) to the current ViewCard shape after
  the card-shape cleanup. The ViewCard a view receives changed: `tagName` became
  `type`, and `attrs`, `text`, `children`, `element`, and the top-level `status`
  were removed — card data now lives in `frontmatter` (parsed YAML fields) and
  `body` (markdown). An agent rewrites each broken view to read the new shape;
  the step is gated by `cb view check` (every view must render) plus a checklist
  the agent must fully work. Run by `cb migrate` as a procedure-kind migration.
steps:
  - id: fix-views
    description: Rewrite every broken view to the new ViewCard interface
    precheck:
      shells:
        - |-
          # Run the fix step if any view fails to render, OR if any view still
          # references a removed ViewCard field. The textual check catches
          # SILENT breakage: a view that reads `card.tagName` (now undefined)
          # renders without throwing but is wrong, so `cb view check` alone
          # would skip it. `.children`/`.text` are too common in React to grep
          # safely; tagName/attrs/element are ViewCard-specific enough.
          if ! cb view check >/dev/null 2>&1; then
            echo "Views fail to render — running the fix step."
          elif ! cb view typecheck >/dev/null 2>&1; then
            echo "Views have type errors against ViewProps — running the fix step."
          elif grep -rEl '\.(tagName|attrs|element)\b' views/ 2>/dev/null | grep -q .; then
            echo "Views still reference removed ViewCard fields — running the fix step."
          else
            exit $CHECK_SKIP
          fi
      whys:
        - All views render, type-check, AND none reference removed ViewCard fields.
    run:
      agents:
        - prompt: |-
            Migrate this box's custom views (views/*.tsx) to the current ViewCard
            interface. The ViewCard a view receives CHANGED:
              - `card.tagName`  → `card.type`
              - `card.status`   → `card.frontmatter?.status`
              - `card.attrs`, `card.text`, `card.children`, `card.element` were
                REMOVED. Card data now lives in `card.frontmatter` (parsed YAML
                fields, minus the body) and `card.body` (the markdown body). The
                old XML element-tree (children/text/attrs of nested elements) is
                gone — the equivalent data is in the card's frontmatter; read an
                actual card of that type to see where each field now lives.

            Maintain a checklist file at
            `config/migration-runs/view-card-shape.checklist.md`. Create it with
            exactly these items as markdown checkboxes, and change `- [ ]` to
            `- [x]` ONLY when that item is genuinely done, appending a one-line
            note of what you changed and where (cite the file):

            - [ ] Ran `cb view check --json` AND `grep -rnE
                  '\.(tagName|attrs|children|text|element)\b|card\.status' views/`
                  to find both views that fail to render AND views that still
                  reference removed fields. NOTE: a view can use `card.tagName`
                  (now undefined) and still render without throwing — it is
                  silently wrong. Fix those too, not just the ones cb view check
                  flags.
            - [ ] Replaced every `card.tagName` with `card.type`.
            - [ ] Replaced every `card.status` with `card.frontmatter?.status`.
            - [ ] For each use of a removed field (`card.attrs`, `card.children`,
                  `card.text`, `card.element`): read a real card of that type,
                  found where the data now lives in `frontmatter`/`body`, and
                  rewrote the view to read it there — PORTING the feature, not
                  deleting it.
            - [ ] Removed any local `ViewCard`/`ViewCardChild` type re-declaration
                  and `as any` cast on card data, so the view is typed against the
                  real ViewProps — this is what lets `cb view typecheck` catch a
                  future field change instead of it failing silently.
            - [ ] `cb view check` AND `cb view typecheck` both pass.

            You control how you work the list — fix views in any order, and loop
            back to an earlier item if a later `cb view check` reveals more. When
            `cb view check` is green and every box is checked, you are done. Do
            NOT check a box you did not actually complete; do NOT satisfy a check
            by deleting functionality.
          # Boxes can have several views, and a heavy one (e.g. a sandbox view
          # with many removed-field refs) eats turns; the default 20 isn't
          # enough. If this still runs out, the run fails cleanly (gate blocks
          # completion) and re-running resumes from the committed partial work.
          max-turns: 60
    validate:
      shells:
        - cb view check
        - cb view typecheck
        - |-
          # Completeness gate: the checklist must exist, have at least one
          # checked box, and have no unchecked boxes left.
          f="config/migration-runs/view-card-shape.checklist.md"
          test -f "$f" && grep -q '\[x\]' "$f" && ! grep -q '\[ \]' "$f"
      severity: abort
      instructions:
        - Every view renders, type-checks against ViewProps, and the checklist is fully worked.
      whys:
        - The migration is only complete when all views render, type-check, and every checklist item is done.
---
